    "At have overvundet en lang sygdom og endelig være erklæret helt rask.": "To have overcome a long illness and finally be declared completely healthy.",
    "At være meget stolt af sig selv, fordi man motionerer hver eneste dag.": "To be very proud of oneself because one exercises every single day.",
    "At føle sig rigtig godt tilpas og være i en situation, man nyder meget.": "To feel really comfortable and be in a situation one enjoys a lot.",
    "At føle sig enormt stærk i kroppen, lige efter man har trænet hårdt.": "To feel enormously strong in the body right after one has trained hard.",
    "At være den person, der altid inspirerer andre til at leve sundt og godt.": "To be the person who always inspires others to live healthily and well.",
    "At være helt fri for smerter i kroppen, fordi man har hvilet sig nok.": "To be completely free of pain in the body because one has rested enough.",
    "Begyndende svækkelse & Inkubation": "Onset of weakness & Incubation",
    "At ligne en hængt kat, at have bly i benene osv.": "To look like a hanged cat (look terrible), to have lead in one's legs, etc.",
    "Man mærker de allerførste tegn på, at man er træt, og man føler sig ikke helt frisk og rask længere.": "One notices the very first signs of being tired, and one does not feel completely fresh and well anymore.",
    "At føle sig meget svag og træt i kroppen uden helt at vide hvorfor.": "To feel very weak and tired in the body without really knowing why.",
    "At have voldsomme smerter i benene efter at have stået op hele dagen.": "To have severe pain in one's legs after standing up all day.",
